      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hurontown%2C_Michigan"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The community sits just south of the city of Houghton, tucked into the Keweenaw Peninsula’s rugged landscape.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hurontown%2C_Michigan"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Hurontown was officially platted in 1862, formalizing the layout that still guides its streets today.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hurontown%2C_Michigan"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The CDP is almost entirely surrounded by Houghton on its west, north, and east sides, making it a quiet enclave within the city.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
